From: Andrew Stellman <astellman@stellman-greene.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:32:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Test that binary cpio refuses a uid or gid above 65535

For the bin and pwb formats, write one entry with uid 65536 and
one with gid 65536 and expect archive_write_header() to return
ARCHIVE_FAILED for both. An entry with uid and gid 65535 must
still be written and read back with those ids.

The issue was found by Claude Opus 5.5 running Quality Playbook, an
LLM-driven code review tool:
https://github.com/andrewstellman/quality-playbook
The fix and this changelog were drafted with Claude Opus 5.5 and
reviewed by me.
